            <ArticleTitle>Herpes zoster: a geriatric disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>41-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Both the incidence and the severity of herpes zoster increase with advancing age. Postherpetic neuralgia may persist for more than a year. Treatment is usually symptomatic, and early corticosteroid therapy should be considered in patients over age 50. Psychotropic drugs also may be indicated to overcome depression.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
